            "concept": "Apply a whole-life-cycle boundary to identify provisional environmental hotspots, burden shifting and qualified trade-offs.",
            "mechanic": "Students map evidence cards onto five life-cycle stages, nominate a provisional hotspot with reasons, then receive a boundary-change card that adds or removes a stage or changes a use, care, repair, lifespan or end-of-life assumption. They must revise or defend their hotspot and qualified judgement.",
            "lesson_placement": "After explicit teaching of the life-cycle lens and before the extended evaluation response.",
